WEBVTT

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.904
(sighs)

00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:12.547
♪ This is for
all the lonely people ♪

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:18.883
♪ Thinking that life
has passed us by ♪

00:00:20.821 --> 00:00:24.490
♪ We won't give up until we ♪

00:00:24.626 --> 00:00:27.661
♪ Drink from the silver cup ♪

00:00:27.796 --> 00:00:32.831
♪ And ride that highway
in the sky. ♪

00:00:34.263 --> 00:00:36.905
Your ukulele skills
are improving.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.203
Thank you.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.469
♪ ♪

00:00:39.604 --> 00:00:41.034
(seabirds calling)

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.902
BRANCH:
Operation Family Harmony

00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:44.840
is on and poppin'!

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:46.373
- What?
- What? Oh, nothing.

00:00:46.508 --> 00:00:48.209
I just... Well,
if I didn't know any better,

00:00:48.344 --> 00:00:49.747
I'd-I'd almost say
you were excited.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.181
Uh, it has nothing to do
with my brothers.

00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:54.682
TINY DIAMOND (over speaker):
All right. All right.

00:00:54.818 --> 00:00:56.423
Tiny, Branch, Poppy

00:00:56.558 --> 00:00:58.519
- and this random dude...
- What?

00:00:58.655 --> 00:01:01.325
...on another musical adventure
filled with heart, hilarity

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.593
and happiness.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.027
Tiny! What are you doing here?

00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:07.168
Well, Aunt Poppy,
for your information,

00:01:07.303 --> 00:01:08.696
I am no longer a baby.

00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:10.363
I am a big boy now.

00:01:10.498 --> 00:01:13.070
And I'm on
a man-sized rite of passage

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:18.140
to learn lessons of life,
courage and maybe love.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:19.909
Aw.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:21.414
Uh, should we be letting
a baby drive?

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.848
Not to worry, fellow grown-up.

00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:25.878
I have procured
my learner's permit.

00:01:26.014 --> 00:01:27.281
Who is Adulty McManface?

00:01:27.416 --> 00:01:31.058
The better question is:
Are you a narc?

00:01:31.194 --> 00:01:32.291
What? No. No.

00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:34.354
(stammers) Why? Are you?

00:01:34.489 --> 00:01:37.195
Enough chitchat,
Adulty McManface. Step on it!

00:01:37.331 --> 00:01:38.961
(roars)

00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:40.765
BRANCH:
<i>Okay, guys, where was I?</i>

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.363
We got to find our brothers
and fast.

00:01:42.498 --> 00:01:44.901
But don't worry,
old Branch has got it handled.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.671
All we have to do
is follow the clues.

00:01:47.806 --> 00:01:50.308
Wow. Check out your old outfits.

00:01:50.444 --> 00:01:51.744
Puffy jackets?

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.877
Puka shell necklaces?
Denim tuxedos?!

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:57.250
Branch, did you have
frosted tips?

00:01:57.386 --> 00:01:58.913
Yeah. It was an era.

00:01:59.049 --> 00:02:01.021
Uh, don't forget his perm.

00:02:01.157 --> 00:02:02.082
No way.

00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:03.853
Pictures or it didn't happen.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:06.027
Aah! Look at you!
You were so cute.

00:02:06.162 --> 00:02:07.523
I love it.

00:02:07.659 --> 00:02:08.960
(sobs, laughs)

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.298
JOHN DORY:
Uh, but we had to pull the plug

00:02:10.433 --> 00:02:12.092
when he tried to frost his perm.

00:02:12.228 --> 00:02:13.695
- (laughing)
- It was an era!

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:15.131
- Tragic.
- Whew.

00:02:15.266 --> 00:02:16.569
While you two are
strolling down memory lane,

00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:18.169
I'll work on finding Spruce.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.406
I'm gonna need copies
of that pic-- wallet size.

00:02:20.541 --> 00:02:22.008
Listen, baby brother,

00:02:22.143 --> 00:02:23.611
we don't need your little board
to find Spruce.

00:02:23.747 --> 00:02:25.609
- It's not little.
- Because I got this.

00:02:25.744 --> 00:02:27.507
Ha! Booyah. (chuckles)

00:02:27.643 --> 00:02:30.151
BRANCH: A postcard that says
"wish you were here"?

00:02:30.286 --> 00:02:31.010
That's it?

00:02:31.146 --> 00:02:32.716
It's not even signed.

00:02:32.851 --> 00:02:34.350
It's definitely Spruce.

00:02:34.486 --> 00:02:36.758
I mean, he's the only one I know
who talks that way.

00:02:36.893 --> 00:02:39.019
There's no return address.
It's blank.

00:02:39.154 --> 00:02:40.692
This could be from anywhere.

00:02:40.828 --> 00:02:42.393
We can't find Spruce with this.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.696
Yeah, we can!

00:02:43.832 --> 00:02:45.632
All we have to do
is find this sunset.

00:02:45.768 --> 00:02:47.829
Liking that optimism,
Poppy Seed.

00:02:47.964 --> 00:02:50.167
Branch, one word: keeper.

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:53.135
Hey, man, I know about
being treated like a baby.

00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:55.276
But while it's just
the two of us,

00:02:55.411 --> 00:02:56.473
you want some of this?

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.173
Nah. Thanks, man.

00:02:58.308 --> 00:02:59.740
I-I can't get back
on that train.

00:02:59.876 --> 00:03:01.244
Suit yourself.

00:03:01.379 --> 00:03:02.915
- I mean, hey, look at this.
- (sucking noisily)

00:03:03.051 --> 00:03:04.278
We're never gonna find Spruce
with this.

00:03:04.414 --> 00:03:07.488
I bet this sunset
doesn't even exist.

00:03:07.623 --> 00:03:09.517
TINY DIAMOND:
Oh, hot dog!

00:03:09.653 --> 00:03:11.059
Ah, man.

00:03:11.194 --> 00:03:12.518
Of course.

00:03:12.654 --> 00:03:14.760
Hey, guys.
You're gonna want to see this.

00:03:14.896 --> 00:03:16.562
- I knew we'd find it.
- (laughs)

00:03:16.698 --> 00:03:18.365
Spruce must be on that island.

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:19.827
Whoa! Easy there, goggles.

00:03:19.962 --> 00:03:20.963
All right, y'all.

00:03:21.098 --> 00:03:21.962
- Let's mobilize.
- Yeah!

00:03:22.098 --> 00:03:23.936
Pedal to the metal, JD.

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:28.169
What are you doing?

00:03:28.304 --> 00:03:29.777
JOHN DORY:
Worry not, friends.

00:03:29.912 --> 00:03:31.372
Rhonda here's
completely waterproof.

00:03:32.446 --> 00:03:34.782
(Rhonda roaring)

00:03:35.384 --> 00:03:38.148
(all screaming)

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:44.686
(motorcycle engine rumbling)

00:03:44.821 --> 00:03:47.454
♪ ♪

00:03:50.428 --> 00:03:53.532
Oh, Grissy, this is
the most romantic honeymoon

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.729
I've ever been on.

00:03:55.864 --> 00:03:57.033
Ever.

00:03:57.169 --> 00:03:59.101
Whoo!
It is a night of surprises.

00:03:59.237 --> 00:04:01.842
- (engine revving)
- Whoa! (chuckles, yells)

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:05.210
To the water park!

00:04:05.346 --> 00:04:07.012
Woo-hoo!

00:04:09.419 --> 00:04:12.079
(Rhonda sputtering)

00:04:12.214 --> 00:04:14.815
(Branch coughing, spitting)

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:16.523
Good old Rhonda.

00:04:16.658 --> 00:04:19.320
Completely waterproof, huh?

00:04:19.456 --> 00:04:20.957
So, um, John Dory,
who wrote that song

00:04:21.092 --> 00:04:22.330
"Girl, I Love Your Love, Girl"?

00:04:22.465 --> 00:04:23.656
- I did.
- Cool.

00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:24.860
Who wrote, um, "Girl,
You Break My Heart, Girl"?

00:04:24.995 --> 00:04:26.459
- I did.
- So cool.

00:04:26.594 --> 00:04:28.066
Who wrote
"Girl, I Love Your Love, Girl,

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.529
"You Break My Heart, Girl,
I Still Love You,

00:04:29.665 --> 00:04:30.834
"But I Seriously Think
We Should Have a Talk

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.133
About Our Relationship, Girl"?

00:04:32.269 --> 00:04:33.566
- Oh, that was Branch.
- Shut up!

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:34.934
That was my favorite
BroZone song, like, ever.

00:04:35.069 --> 00:04:36.241
JK. Also me.

00:04:36.377 --> 00:04:37.137
(laughs)

00:04:37.272 --> 00:04:39.411
Branch has never written a song.

00:04:39.547 --> 00:04:40.948
I was a baby.

00:04:41.083 --> 00:04:42.549
What did you want me
to write about, diaper rash?

00:04:42.684 --> 00:04:45.248
Okay, take it easy, Bitty B.

00:04:46.317 --> 00:04:47.784
- (Branch groans)
- Hey, what's wrong?

00:04:47.919 --> 00:04:49.085
Nothing. Super happy.

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.187
This is our most fun
mission yet. Yay.

00:04:51.323 --> 00:04:54.290
Branch, do you know
how lucky you are?

00:04:54.425 --> 00:04:56.193
A brother is a friend
who can never leave you.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:57.999
It's the strongest bond
in the world.

00:04:58.134 --> 00:05:00.327
I would kill to have a sibling
to sing with, Branch.

00:05:00.463 --> 00:05:03.303
(scoffs)
Yeah, well, you can have mine.

00:05:03.438 --> 00:05:05.404
Okay. Fine.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:07.001
Poppy, wait.

00:05:07.137 --> 00:05:09.003
(sighs) Grown-up stuff.

00:05:09.138 --> 00:05:10.571
Am I right? (chuckles)

00:05:10.707 --> 00:05:12.375
You know, I still got
that thang, if you want it.

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:16.015
Whoa, whoa. Don't be waving
that thing around.

00:05:17.178 --> 00:05:18.412
All right, y'all.

00:05:18.548 --> 00:05:19.915
We're getting close
to something.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.923
I can feel it. (gasps)

00:05:23.058 --> 00:05:25.587
- (all scream)
- Whoa. What do we got here?

00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:28.755
Hey, guys, looks like I found
some fellow rock climbers.

00:05:28.891 --> 00:05:29.825
Hi.

00:05:29.961 --> 00:05:31.994
Welcome to Vacay Island,

00:05:32.129 --> 00:05:34.966
where every day is a vacay.

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:39.170
♪ When you're on a holiday ♪

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:43.176
♪ You can't find
the words to say ♪

00:05:43.312 --> 00:05:47.847
- ♪ On an island in the sun ♪
- (playful chatter)

00:05:47.982 --> 00:05:51.949
♪ We'll be playing, having fun ♪

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:55.052
♪ And it makes me feel so fine ♪

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:59.656
♪ I can't control my brain ♪

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:00.925
♪ Ah! ♪

00:06:01.061 --> 00:06:02.926
♪ She call me Mr. Boombastic ♪

00:06:03.061 --> 00:06:04.660
♪ Tell me fantastic ♪

00:06:04.796 --> 00:06:07.566
♪ Touch me on the back,
she says I'm Mr. Ro-o... ♪

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.629
♪ Smooth ♪

00:06:10.671 --> 00:06:12.768
♪ Sailing ♪

00:06:12.903 --> 00:06:18.842
♪ Takes me away to where
I've always heard it could be ♪

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:21.246
POPPY:
Heartthrob.

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:24.410
♪ Just a dream and the wind
to carry me ♪

00:06:24.545 --> 00:06:30.221
♪ And soon I will be free. ♪

